 "answer": {
  "answer": "The code counts four settings as confirmed challenging cases (S2, S5, S10, S29), so the goal of five was not met. But none of the four is a confirmed case of VaVAM rear-ending a slowed lead car. At S2, S10 and S29 every failure was a front contact logged before or at the moment the policy took control, while the ego was still replaying the recorded drive. Those failures come from the retimed lead car overlapping the logged ego, not from the policy. S5 is a real policy failure, but it is a sideswipe into a car in the left lane after the policy steered against a RIGHT command, not a rear-end. It also used a 350 ms planner delay, above the brief's 200 ms limit, and S10 and S29 also exceed that limit. Where the policy itself failed (S4, S5, one run at S15, and possibly S8), the pattern was drifting left into an adjacent car, not failing to brake. Apart from S5, each of these rests on one or two runs, so they are hints rather than rates.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "On scene 023b7fcc, with the lead car shifted +1.5 s at 0.75x speed and 50 ms delay, every run failed. Triage puts all of them on the replay: the lead car's box already overlapped the ego from 2.7 s, during log replay, before the 4.7 s handoff. These are not policy failures and do not show a rear-end by VaVAM.",
    "settings": [
     "S2"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On scene 09a95ffa, every run at +1.5 s, 0.75x and 250 ms delay failed. All of them were front contacts set up while the ego was still replaying the recorded path, before the policy took over at 4.6 s. The setting is also above the 200 ms limit.",
    "settings": [
     "S10"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On scene 12855a41, every run at +0.5 s, 0.5x and 400 ms delay failed. Each was a front contact with lead car 5 flagged at the handoff instant, with the ego still on the recorded path, so it is a replay artifact. The 400 ms delay is twice the brief's limit.",
    "settings": [
     "S29"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On scene 096988dd at -2 s, 1.5x and 350 ms delay, every run failed through the policy's own error. It steered left against a RIGHT command and sideswiped vehicle 22 in the adjacent lane. This is a confirmed policy failure, but not a rear-end, and it is above the 200 ms limit. The runs are flagged as possible artifacts because the ego ended up far off the recorded path, and triage attributes that drift to the policy.",
    "settings": [
     "S5"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "Retiming the lead car while the ego is still replaying the log can produce a front collision before the policy takes control. That happened in the single runs at S7 and S9 as well as in every run at S2, S10 and S29. These failures say nothing about the policy.",
